PrepFlow
User Flow & Application Workflow

Version: v1.0

Status: Draft

Author: Tejas Nere

1. Purpose

This document defines how users interact with PrepFlow from the moment they open the application until they complete their learning journey.

The objective is to ensure a smooth, intuitive, and distraction-free experience for both students and administrators.

2. User Types

The platform currently supports two user roles:

Student
Administrator

Each user follows a different workflow.

3. Student Journey

Student opens PrepFlow

↓

Dashboard

↓

Select Subject

↓

Select Chapter

↓

Open Resource

↓

Complete Resource

↓

Progress Updates

↓

Continue Next Resource

↓

Complete Chapter

↓

Complete Subject

↓

Complete Overall Learning Journey

4. Student Dashboard Flow

When the student opens PrepFlow, the dashboard should immediately display:

Overall Progress
Continue Learning
Subject Cards
Search
Analytics
Recently Opened Chapters

The student should immediately understand where to continue.

5. Subject Flow

Student selects a subject.

The system displays:

Subject Progress
Chapter List
Search Within Subject

Each chapter card should show:

Chapter Name
Progress
Completed Resources
Continue Button
6. Chapter Flow

Student opens a chapter.

The chapter page displays:

Chapter Information
Progress
Learning Checklist
Resources

Each resource appears as an independent item.

7. Resource Flow

Student selects a resource.

↓

Resource opens.

↓

Student studies.

↓

Student marks resource as completed.

↓

Progress updates automatically.

↓

Student returns to chapter.

↓

Next recommended resource is highlighted.

8. Progress Flow

Resource Completed

↓

Chapter Progress Updated

↓

Subject Progress Updated

↓

Overall Progress Updated

↓

Dashboard Analytics Updated

The student should never manually calculate progress.

9. Search Flow

Student opens search.

↓

Searches:

Subject

Chapter

Resource

↓

Results displayed instantly.

↓

Student opens desired content.

10. Analytics Flow

Dashboard Analytics display:

Overall Completion

↓

Subject Completion

↓

Chapter Completion

↓

Learning Progress

Analytics update automatically after every completed resource.

11. Continue Learning Flow

When returning to PrepFlow:

Dashboard

↓

Continue Learning

↓

Previously Opened Chapter

↓

Previously Incomplete Resource

↓

Resume Learning

Students should never search for where they stopped.

12. Admin Journey

Administrator

↓

Login

↓

Dashboard

↓

Manage Content

↓

Publish

↓

Students View Updated Content

No deployment should be required.

13. Admin Dashboard Flow

After login, the administrator should see:

Total Subjects
Total Chapters
Total Resources
Draft Content
Published Content
Recent Updates
