25. Error Flow

Whenever an error occurs:

Display meaningful message.

Allow retry.

Never display technical errors to students.

26. Empty State Flow

Whenever no content exists:

Display informative message.

Examples:

"No Resources Available"

"No Notes Uploaded"

"Chapter Coming Soon"

27. Success Flow

Every completed action should provide immediate feedback.

Examples:

Resource Completed

Progress Updated

Chapter Completed

Subject Completed

Animations should remain subtle.

28. User Experience Principles

Students should never feel lost.

Students should never search unnecessarily.

Students should never wonder what to study next.

Administrators should never modify code.

Administrators should never edit the database manually.

29. Final Workflow Philosophy

Students

Learn

↓

Complete

↓

Track

↓

Repeat

Administrators

Create

↓

Manage

↓

Publish

↓

Improve

30. Final Statement

Every workflow inside PrepFlow is designed around simplicity.

The application should guide students through their learning journey while allowing administrators to continuously improve the platform without software development.